            ],
            datasheet: "W128 SLICE32 - 32-bit CPU slice\n\nFour slices side by side make the 128-bit datapath (a bit-slice design, like the bit-slice processors of the 1970s). Each holds bits 32k..32k+31 of all registers (RegFile32) and of the ALU (ALU32).\n\n- Y: ALU result (written back to register RD when WE = 1)\n- DOUT: register RB (store data)\n- G / P: slice carry generate / propagate, to the board\'s CLA4; CIN comes back from it\n- A0 / A31: lowest / highest bit of operand A, the shift-in of the neighbouring slices (SLI / SRI)\n- Z: the 32 result bits are all 0",
            hash: 7699296457923364292,
