            datasheet: "W128 CONTROL UNIT - hardwired control\n\nState machine (two flip-flops): FETCH (IR = ROM[PC], PC = PC + 1) -> EXEC -> (LD/ST: MEM) -> FETCH; HALT -> HALT. RST (synchronous) returns to FETCH at PC 0.\n\nEXEC: ALU instructions write RD and the flags; LD/ST compute ra + imm into MAR; jumps load PC with imm[7:0] when the condition holds. MEM: LD writes the memory word into RD; ST pulses WSTB during the low half of the clock.\n\nOutputs: register selects (RA, RB, RD from IR), WE, the ALU controls (operand select SREG/SIMM/SMEM, SUB, one-hot operation OSUM..OPB), PC, MAR, WSTB, IR and the state / flag lines for the LEDs.",
            hash: 18232412666085473686,
